Branch kind (`kind` discriminator):
- CONDITIONAL — default branch kind on EXCLUSIVE and INCLUSIVE decisions. Example: `{kind: "CONDITIONAL", id: "br-yes", label: "Eligible", condition: "score >= 750"}`.
- DEFAULT — keywords: otherwise, for every other case, catch-all, anything else, for all remaining cases, none of the above apply. NO condition; label describes the destination. Example: `{kind: "DEFAULT", id: "br-fallback", label: "Manual review"}`. At most one DEFAULT per decision, and it needs at least one CONDITIONAL sibling.
- UNCONDITIONAL — Example: `{kind: "UNCONDITIONAL", id: "br-track-a", label: "IT prep"}`.
- EVENT_GATEWAY — branch of an EVENT_BASED decision. Carries `triggerKind` (TIMER | MESSAGE) and a required `triggerDetail` (a duration for TIMER or a message name for MESSAGE) in place of a condition. Example: `{kind: "EVENT_GATEWAY", id: "br-confirmed", label: "Payment confirmed", triggerKind: "MESSAGE", triggerDetail: "payment confirmation"}`.
- Kind/decision matching is strict: CONDITIONAL and DEFAULT on EXCLUSIVE and INCLUSIVE decisions; UNCONDITIONAL only on PARALLEL decisions; EVENT_GATEWAY only on EVENT_BASED decisions.
- An INCLUSIVE decision whose branches can ALL be false needs a DEFAULT branch for the "none applied" path — that path is a branch like any other, not an unlabelled edge. Example: two optional add-on services, plus `{kind: "DEFAULT", id: "br-no-add-ons", label: "No add-ons selected"}` routing straight to the next step.
